x86_64-linux  two differences, both older than this case. The implicit constructors and destructors - _ZN4BothC1Ev, _ZN4BothD1Ev, _ZN5FirstC1Ev, _ZN6SecondC1Ev - are ordinary definitions here and comdat linkonce_odr in clang's, as dynamic-cast.nonames records. And clang emits _ZTI4Both and _ZTS4Both where cxx1 emits neither: `Both` has two bases, so describing it to the run time needs __vmi_class_type_info, which this compiler refuses by name, and the vtable's type_info slot is a plain zero instead. Measured, and it is why this case is still correct: `dynamic_cast<void *>` reads offset-to-top, the slot two words in front of the address point, and cxx1 writes 0 and -16 there exactly as clang does. It never reads the type_info slot, which is the null one. A `dynamic_cast<Both *>` would need that slot and is refused by name before it can look.
arm64-darwin  the same two, one constructor fewer: __ZN5FirstC1Ev and __ZN6SecondC1Ev, plus the missing __ZTI4Both and __ZTS4Both.
